          "turn_index": 2,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Does it ever go back to normal?",
          "answer": "The retrieved guidance does not directly answer whether an underactive thyroid returns to normal.\n\nThe *Hypothyroidism (underactive thyroid)* summary lists several causes, including autoimmune thyroiditis, thyroid surgery, radioactive iodine treatment, neck radiotherapy, and some medicines. It also mentions \"the recovery phase after some forms of thyroiditis.\" That suggests the thyroid can recover in some situations, but the summary does not explain which cases, how often, or what that would look like for you.\n\nYour clinician can tell you what is likely for your situation. Useful questions include:\n\n- What is the cause of my underactive thyroid, as far as we know?\n- Could it improve over time, or is it likely to be long-term?\n- Will I need a repeat test to see whether it has changed?\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
